config BR2_PACKAGE_ATV329Q_SCREEN
	bool "atv329q display (MDP3 -> DSI -> ADV7533 HDMI)"
	default y
	help
	  Display support for the atv329q: the kernel side (DRM/KMS with fbdev
	  emulation, framebuffer console, boot logo -- all already enabled in
	  board/geniatech/atv329q/linux.config) plus the userland side:

	    - /etc/init.d/S15screen, the oracle-gated DPMS re-arm helper (it
	      reads the ADV7533 lock oracle with busybox's i2cget applet),
	    - a getty on tty0, i.e. a login prompt on the HDMI screen.

	  Disable for a headless box: the package then merges its
	  linux-noscreen.config kernel fragment, which drops DRM/FB/fbcon/logo
	  from the kernel, and installs none of the userland. Access stays over
	  SSH (eth0/wlan0) and the serial console.

	  The kernel patches (MDP3 driver, DSI, ADV7533, MDSS clock, device
	  tree) are always applied -- they are the board's source of truth.
	  This only controls whether the display is built and used.

	  Note: the kernel differs between on and off, so run
	  `./build.sh kernel` after flipping this.
